    <H2>Microsoft CoPilot</H2>
        <P1>

            According to Microsoft, “A copilot is a conversational, 
            AI-powered assistant that helps boost productivity and 
            streamline workflows by offering contextual assistance, 
            automating routine tasks, and analyzing data.”   

            Copilot was made to boost productivity, simplify automation,
            and provide contextual intelligence in Windows, Bing, Edge,
            and Microsoft 365. It is used in different ways across the
            Microsoft family of products. For example in Word it can 
            help you save time on writing tasks by helping you draft 
            and revise your work. While in Microsoft Azure it can provide
             AI-assisted code suggestions on project such as developing apps. </P1>

     <H2>Popular Uses: </H2>
        <ul>
            <li>Creation</li>
            <li>Data Analysis</li>
            <li>Project Management</li>
            <li>Communication</li>
        </ul> 
           

            <p1>Copilot uses Natural Language Processing and Machine Learning
             Algorithms. This allows it to understand and respond to commands 
             through everyday language and analyze activities  to provide
              better outputs based on the users previous actions. Copilot 
              aims to reduce manual effort, enhance the decision-making
               process. </p1>

